<div class="container">
      <div id="paragraph-4869-1" class="Accordion row" data-allow-toggle>
              <div class="medium-4 box-accordion">
          <h3>
      <button class="box-accordion-top Accordion-trigger"
            aria-label="Developing a Food Safety Plan"
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="accordion-content-4863"
            id="accordion-4863">

            
    Developing a Food Safety Plan
    <div class="box-accordion-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      </button>
</h3>
<div id="accordion-content-4863"
      class="Accordion-panel"
      aria-labelledby="accordion-4863"
      aria-hidden="true"
      hidden>
      <p>
        
  <p>A food safety plan is a requirement for any specialty crop operation or group undergoing formal food safety certification.&nbsp;</p><p>FSCSC will cover a percentage of the following food safety plan development expenses:</p><ul><li>The cost of specialty crop operations developing their own plan, including costs of seminars and tools used to create a food safety plan.</li><li>The cost of hiring a consultant, including consulting fees, and other associated expenses.</li></ul><p>For each eligible program year, FSCSC will cover eligible expenses as follows:&nbsp;<strong>75 percent (no maximum)</strong>.&nbsp;</p><p>Expected FSCSC payments for each eligible year will equal the applicant’s eligible expenses multiplied by the corresponding percentage, not to exceed the category’s maximum payment amount. This amount, plus any additional cost share assistance received, cannot exceed the total amount of the eligible expense.&nbsp;</p>

      </p>
</div>
        </div>
              <div class="medium-4 box-accordion">
          <h3>
      <button class="box-accordion-top Accordion-trigger"
            aria-label="Maintaining or Updating a Food Safety Plan"
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="accordion-content-4864"
            id="accordion-4864">

            
    Maintaining or Updating a Food Safety Plan
    <div class="box-accordion-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      </button>
</h3>
<div id="accordion-content-4864"
      class="Accordion-panel"
      aria-labelledby="accordion-4864"
      aria-hidden="true"
      hidden>
      <p>
        
  <p>Certification programs typically require an annual review of the food safety plan to ensure it is current and addresses any new audit or regulatory requirements, as well as incorporates any new hazards. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>FSCSC will cover a percentage of the costs of maintaining and updating existing food safety plans. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>For each eligible program year, FSCSC will cover eligible expenses as follows: <strong>75 percent, up to a maximum of $675</strong>.</p><p>Expected FSCSC payments for each eligible year will equal the applicant’s eligible expenses multiplied by the corresponding percentage, not to exceed the category’s maximum payment amount. This amount, plus any additional cost share assistance received, cannot exceed the total amount of the eligible expense.</p>

      </p>
</div>
        </div>
              <div class="medium-4 box-accordion">
          <h3>
      <button class="box-accordion-top Accordion-trigger"
            aria-label="Food Safety Certification"
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="accordion-content-4865"
            id="accordion-4865">

            
    Food Safety Certification
    <div class="box-accordion-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      </button>
</h3>
<div id="accordion-content-4865"
      class="Accordion-panel"
      aria-labelledby="accordion-4865"
      aria-hidden="true"
      hidden>
      <p>
        
  <p>FSCSC will cover a percentage of the cost of obtaining food safety certification issued by a certifier. This includes:</p><ul><li>Application fees </li><li>Inspection costs</li><li>Inspection fees (including travel costs and per diem for certifiers)</li><li>User fees or certifier sales assessments </li><li>Postage</li></ul><p>For each eligible program year, FSCSC will cover eligible expenses as follows: <strong>75 percent, up to a maximum of $2,000</strong>.</p><p>Expected FSCSC payments for each eligible year will equal the applicant’s eligible expenses multiplied by the corresponding percentage, not to exceed the category’s maximum payment amount. This amount, plus any additional cost share assistance received, cannot exceed the total amount of the eligible expense.&nbsp;</p>

      </p>
</div>
        </div>
          </div>
    <br>
      <div id="paragraph-4869-2" class="Accordion row" data-allow-toggle>
              <div class="medium-4 box-accordion">
          <h3>
      <button class="box-accordion-top Accordion-trigger"
            aria-label="Certification Upload Fees"
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="accordion-content-4866"
            id="accordion-4866">

            
    Certification Upload Fees
    <div class="box-accordion-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      </button>
</h3>
<div id="accordion-content-4866"
      class="Accordion-panel"
      aria-labelledby="accordion-4866"
      aria-hidden="true"
      hidden>
      <p>
        
  <p>FSCSC will cover a percentage of the cost to upload audit reports and certification documentation into commercial audit databases, which may be required by buyers of specialty crops.&nbsp;</p><p>For each eligible program year, FSCSC will cover eligible expenses as follows: <strong>75 percent, up to a maximum of $375</strong>.</p><p>Expected FSCSC payments for each eligible year will equal the applicant’s eligible expenses multiplied by the corresponding percentage, not to exceed the category’s maximum payment amount. This amount, plus any additional cost share assistance received, cannot exceed the total amount of the eligible expense.</p>

      </p>
</div>
        </div>
              <div class="medium-4 box-accordion">
          <h3>
      <button class="box-accordion-top Accordion-trigger"
            aria-label="Microbiological Testing"
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="accordion-content-4867"
            id="accordion-4867">

            
    Microbiological Testing
    <div class="box-accordion-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      </button>
</h3>
<div id="accordion-content-4867"
      class="Accordion-panel"
      aria-labelledby="accordion-4867"
      aria-hidden="true"
      hidden>
      <p>
        
  <p>FSCSC will cover a percentage of the microbiological testing for products, soil amendments, and water as specified by a food safety plan or food safety management system.</p><p>For each eligible program year and each category (products, soil amendments and water), FSCSC will cover eligible expenses as follows: <strong>75 percent, up to five tests</strong>, including postage.</p><p>Expected FSCSC payments for each eligible year will equal the applicant’s eligible expenses for each category (products, soil amendments and water) multiplied by the corresponding percentage, not to exceed the category’s maximum number of tests. This amount, plus any additional cost share assistance received, cannot exceed the total amount of the eligible expense.&nbsp;</p>

      </p>
</div>
        </div>
              <div class="medium-4 box-accordion">
          <h3>
      <button class="box-accordion-top Accordion-trigger"
            aria-label="Training Expenses"
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="accordion-content-4868"
            id="accordion-4868">

            
    Training Expenses
    <div class="box-accordion-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      </button>
</h3>
<div id="accordion-content-4868"
      class="Accordion-panel"
      aria-labelledby="accordion-4868"
      aria-hidden="true"
      hidden>
      <p>
        
  <p>FSCSC will cover the cost of food safety training for specialty crop operations.</p><p>For each eligible program year, FSCSC will cover eligible expenses as follows: <strong>100 percent, up to a maximum of $500</strong>.</p><p>Expected FSCSC payments for each eligible year will equal the applicant’s eligible expenses multiplied by the corresponding percentage, not to exceed the category’s maximum payment amount. This amount, plus any additional cost share assistance received, cannot exceed the total amount of the eligible expense.&nbsp;</p>

      </p>
</div>
